Z||000010||Master_Sushi||12-20-2001||11:39 PM||||The fiero isn't the most easy car to pull a nice drift in. I've done it myself a few times in mine though. Just be carefull the back end dosent come around on you. If it does its pretty hard to get back under control. Might end up drifting into a curb or other object. lol||||reg||1
Z||000011||artherd||12-21-2001||04:51 AM||||I've got my car setup pretty well, it will drift when pushed to the limit, and touching it into over or understeer can be had by modulating the throttle alone.<P>Lots of fun.  Scary at 40mph in second...<P>Best place for it is on an autocross or proper race track.   Like George said, you get to do it ALL DAY and you won't risk hurting people!<P>My god, mid-engine cars are SO MUCH FUN!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: Watch that tail though, these cars require you to DRIVE them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
